  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Established in 1927, the University of Bridgeport (UB) is a private university in Bridgeport, Connecticut. Originally founded as the Junior College of Connecticut, it became a four-year university in 1947.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>UB is known for its diverse student population, with over 5000 students representing various backgrounds and cultures. The University has a vibrant campus life with more than 100 student organisations and clubs, and hosts several cultural events and support services for international students.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>UB provides multiple on-campus housing options for undergraduate and graduate students. The University has several residence halls with modern amenities.</p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><i>Additionally, if you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to </i><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\"><i>download our app</i></a><i> and check out the Stays feature!</i></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>The Wahlstrom Library at the campus has extensive resources, including books, journals, and digital media, along with study spaces.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong><br>UB boasts modern athletic facilities, including a fitness centre, outdoor fields, and gymnasiums. The University also competes in NCAA Division II sports as the Purple Knights, in basketball, soccer, swimming, and more.</p><p><strong>Laboratory</strong><br>The University has state-of-the-art laboratories for various disciplines. Some key labs include the Applied Computational Fluid Dynamics Lab, Cloud Computing Cluster Controls Lab, Biomedical Research Centre, Health Sciences Research Lab, Nanobiomaterials Engineering Lab, and many more.</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong><br>The University’s main dining hall – the Marina Dining Hall – is UB’s key dining location with a wide range of food options and meal plans for different budgets. You can also visit the Knights End at the John J. Cox Student Centre for healthy and made-to-order options including salads and fruit smoothies. You can also grab snacks and beverages from several eateries on campus.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
